ot used to get into the park itself  ideally this Park is not going to be  that big because I do want to watch out  and not create too many series because  I've already got so much stuff running  at the moment but yeah for that reason  it's just got that main gaits to get  into the park and then the sites here  will be used for more you know kind of  important  things that you might need otherwise  like park information or toilets or I  forgot what I put in that other thing  but it was something like first aid I  believe so it's really that sort of  stuff that you need around up like  entrance which I'm putting in the wings  of the building but only the gates will  actually be used as the park entrance  itself I did realize that in this  episode at least I forgot to put some  turnstiles into the gates so people  might actually be able to walk straight  into the park that's something which I  would definitely have to fix at some  later points but for now just assume  that that Gates has some turnstiles in  it or something like that  in any case moving to the side of the  building and here I think it becomes  quite apparent that this is not just an  adventure building and that I'm not just  using the adventure pieces in a way that  they're supposed to be used because it's  a little bit the fantasy like and I kind  of want to give a shout out to Leonidas  here who's been a huge inspiration for  me ever since I started making videos  he's got a lot of really amazing stuff  in rollercoaster country he hasn't been  active in years in the community I  believe but it's still really great  stuff that even today is really cool to  look back at and his work always  featured a lot of and yeah there you go  spires so that's probably where that  thing comes from and you had a bunch of  projects where he would take different  types of fantasy like elements and  combine them all with a spire castle  like set up and in this case I wanted to  try something very similar even if this  